---
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.docs;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <ContentCard>
    <p class="section-kicker">Documentation</p>
    <h2>Start with an investigation you can inspect</h2>
    <p>Open a synthetic case in the Investigation Lab, inspect the definition and its record, then export the bundle. The same candidate contract applies to a human investigating an agent and an agent assisting with a conventional identity incident.</p>
    <p class="cta-group"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/investigation-lab/">Open Investigation Lab</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/implement/">Run the validator locally</a></p>

    <h2>Build with Core</h2>
    <p>Start with the <a href="/review/">frozen technical review package</a>. The candidate and preserved legacy releases are on the default branch, with separate identities. Use the pinned review snapshot when reporting findings.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Use it to</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/core/">Core 0.1.0-draft.1</a></td><td>Find the pinned contract, schemas, binding, examples, and validation coverage.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/founding/01-core-contract.md">Logical Core contract</a></td><td>Review the 38 proposed requirements independently of an implementation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/implement/">Implementation guide</a></td><td>Validate the examples and scope your own integration.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/conformance/">Validation and conformance</a></td><td>Distinguish reference checks from an independently demonstrated interoperability claim.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/extensions/">Profiles and extensions</a></td><td>Add domain and organization context without changing Core meaning.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/ai-reliability/">Human and agent investigations</a></td><td>Represent attribution, disagreement, policy, and authority explicitly.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Understand the model</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Definition:</strong> a versioned question and its evidence and assessment criteria.</li>
      <li><strong>Question instance:</strong> that question applied to a particular subject, time, and parameters.</li>
      <li><strong>Record:</strong> attributed evidence references, observations, hypotheses, assessments, decisions, and actions.</li>
      <li><strong>Revision:</strong> a new entry preserving the old one and identifying dependent decisions that need review.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>An assessment can be applicable, not applicable, or unresolved. Only an applicable assessment has a <code>yes</code>, <code>no</code>, or <code>unknown</code> outcome. Missing evidence does not mean “no.” A recorded action does not grant permission to execute it.</p>

    <h2>Review the public standard</h2>
    <p><a href="/founding/00-charter.md">Charter</a> · <a href="/governance/">Governance</a> · <a href="/standards/">Standards crosswalk</a> · <a href="/founding/05-review-plan.md">Review plan</a> · <a href="/founding/06-change-and-decision-register.md">Change and decision register</a></p>

    <h2>Work with earlier TENSOR content</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/graphs/">working graph</a> exposes draft questions, routes, and evidence criteria. Investigation Lab’s <strong>Recorded path</strong> shows explicit case transitions and retained assessments. The <a href="/questions/">question catalog</a> and <a href="/studio/">legacy Graph Studio</a> preserve the earlier graph model. Its schemas and version numbers are separate from this candidate. A legacy graph is not a complete Core investigation record.</p>
  </ContentCard>
</BaseLayout>
